From 46e682f47caa3e3b0dff8aa1b67117446be5a775 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:01:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Docs: the aggregation multigrid of AmgX does not converge on
 the elasticity

Measured on the beam of the benchmark of the linear solvers (56,355
unknowns): no convergence in 2000 iterations with the conjugate gradients
of MFEM and of AmgX, nor with FGMRES, while it converges in 18 iterations
on the Laplace equation. Its aggregates ignore the components of the
unknowns and the rigid body modes.
---
 docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst b/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst
index 642d2bc11a..4fe3052df6 100644
--- a/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst
+++ b/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst
@@ -861,8 +861,11 @@ host at each setup, and the resolutions start from a zero initial guess.
        :code:`PCG_AGGREGATION_JACOBI` of :code:`AmgX`: aggregates of size
        two, three post-smoothing sweeps of a damped Jacobi smoother and no
        pre-smoothing sweep, a cycle which is not symmetric, but with which
-       the conjugate gradients converge, as in the configuration of
-       :code:`AmgX`).
+       the conjugate gradients converge on scalar problems, as in the
+       configuration of :code:`AmgX`). Its aggregates ignore the
+       components of the unknowns and the rigid body modes: on the linear
+       elasticity of a beam, it does not converge in 2000 iterations, with
+       the conjugate gradients or FGMRES.
    * - :code:`AmgXParameters`
      - Parameters of :code:`AmgX`, with their names in :code:`AmgX`, which
        complete or override the default configuration. A name without
